{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A fruitful son is Joseph.</b> The reason for the doubling is to say that he is worthy of fruitfulness for two reasons: the first, in that he is Joseph, as they said of blessed memory (Sotah 36b) — Joseph was worthy to establish twelve tribes; and the second, ״a fruitful son over the eye״ — because he did not go astray after his eyes." "And its saying <b>daughters tread upon</b> is explained according to what they said of blessed memory (Tanchuma) — that the wife of Potiphar summoned all the wives of the nobles and great men and brought Joseph in to serve before them, and their gathering and encircling was like this stepping, <b>upon the wall</b> in order to gaze at him. Nevertheless, the holy spirit testifies about him that he did not look upon iniquity, and just as he did not look at them, so too may the evil eye not have dominion over him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:48.730510331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}